course: dictionary
lesson: 5269
title: Joyful: happy, celebrating, and praising
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Joyful means very happy, or full of joy. Joy is a big, bright kind of happy, the feeling you get at a party or a wedding.
explain: The word can also describe things that cause joy. «Joyful news» is news that makes people happy, and «a joyful occasion» is a happy time to celebrate. To check, swap in happy: if the sentence still makes sense, joyful means something like happy.
explain: In church, joyful is used in hymns and prayers for happy praise of God, as in «Make a joyful noise to the Lord». Here it means singing and praising with gladness, not just feeling happy inside.
fact: Joyful is an adjective: joyful, more joyful, most joyful.
fact: The adverb is joyfully, which means in a joyful way.
fact: «Joyful» means very happy, or full of joy.
fact: «Joyful» can also mean causing joy, as in «joyful news».
fact: In church, «joyful» means happy praise of God, as in Psalm 100.
exercise: «Eid al-Fitr is the joyful festival at the end of Ramadan.» What does joyful mean here? | Lost and cold | Very sad and quiet | Short and rude | *Very happy, full of celebration
exercise: The news was «joyful news» for the whole village. What does joyful mean here? | Hard to read | *Causing joy, making people happy | Very old and dusty | Causing fear and worry
exercise: Psalm 100 says «Make a joyful noise to the Lord.» In this line, what does joyful mean? | Loud and angry shouting | Quiet whispering in bed | *Happy singing and praise to God | A party with food and games
test: Which word fits best? «The family had a ___ wedding, full of laughter and dancing.» | Gloomy | Barely | *Joyful | Curt
test: Joyfully means what? | Without any feeling at all | In a slow and sleepy way | *In a happy, joyful way | Angrily
exam: Read «It is all right to be happy, have a party or laugh while sad things happen far away; you can be kind and joyful at once.» What does joyful mean? | Angry and unkind | *Full of joy, even while sad things happen elsewhere | Joyful means the same as sad | Quiet and sleepy
